If it's just the sample information you care about then why not do something like the following?

library(mirt)
dat <- key2binary(SAT12,
                  key = c(1,4,5,2,3,1,2,1,3,1,2,4,2,1,5,3,4,4,1,4,3,3,4,1,3,5,1,3,1,5,4,5))
mod <- mirt(dat, 1)
fs <- fscores(mod)

theta <- 2.295489
mean(fs < theta)
[1] 0.9883333

And no, you don't know that 2.295 should have a probability of 1. Even under the theoretical normal this is

pnorm(theta)
[1] 0.9891474

Phil

